PUBLIC RESPONSE: {E

The entity test in NI 45-106 s. 1.1 requires either net assets of at least C$5 M on the most recent financial statements or that every beneficial owner of an interest is itself an AI. E meets neither: Alex’s C$900 k net financial assets and Bob’s sub-threshold income plus negative net worth disqualify the “all owners are AIs” route, while the partial snapshot (C$5.5 M GIC less C$300 k liabilities) leaves the carrying value and related obligations of the investment properties unaccounted for, so net assets on the financial statements cannot be confirmed at or above the threshold.

By contrast, A’s limited partnership satisfies the “every owner is an AI” route on its face. Each of the three limited partners clears an individual asset test, and the general-partner corporation—capitalized at C$6 M—itself meets the entity net-asset test. The fact that the C$6 M was gifted does not alter the GP’s own balance-sheet position or the status of its owners; nothing in the facts indicates any disqualifying holder. B, C and D likewise satisfy recognized routes (combined spousal income, combined net assets, and the C$10 M contribution giving the D corporation net assets well above C$5 M). The only choice that fails every enumerated path on the supplied facts is therefore E.}

